  "body": "If I do `history.back()`, and when the browser fetches that URL (with the history-navigation flag set on the request), if the response is an HTTP 3xx, should the resulting post-redirect request also have the history-navigation flag said?  Right now it does not, right?\r\n\r\nThis is relevant for both serviceworker bits and the behavior of https://github.com/w3c/navigation-timing/issues/115",
